# Architecture

- Flutter application shell (bootstrap, Firebase, journey, economy, monetization, non-gameplay UI).
- Unity optional presentation-only gameplay runtime (3D board/VFX/environments); never a rules engine.
- Riverpod for application/UI state only.
- Drift/SQLite for local persistence.
- Firebase-first/serverless-first MVP.
- Hybrid bridge contracts: `packages/unity_bridge_contracts` (pure Dart). Default presentation: Flutter 2D until Unity is confirmed ready. See `docs/architecture/FLUTTER_UNITY_HYBRID_ARCHITECTURE_v1.0.md`.

`game_engine` must be pure Dart and must not depend on Flutter UI, Riverpod, Firebase, AdMob, IAP, Drift implementation, HTTP, or analytics SDKs.

`game_solver` must be compatible with authoritative Game Engine rules.

`level_generator` may depend on Game Engine + Solver and must never bypass Solver acceptance.

Avoid premature microservices, Kubernetes, Redis, brokers, and always-on compute.
